WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.583
SPEAKER 1: Hi.

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:02.340
In this video, we
are going to walk you

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:05.160
through a demo of
Contact Center AI that

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.020
helps states and
local governments

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.762
roll out COVID
vaccines effectively.

00:00:09.762 --> 00:00:10.470
SPEAKER 2: Hello.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:14.370
I'm a Virtual Agent for the
State COVID-19 Response Center.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.930
I can help you
determine when you

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.690
will be eligible for
the COVID-19 vaccine,

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.920
and where you can
get vaccinated.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.250
How can I help you?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.790
SPEAKER 1: Is the vaccine free?

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.280
SPEAKER 2: Yes, the
COVID-19 vaccines

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.320
will be available at no cost.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.120
What else can I help you with?

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.280
SPEAKER 1: Do COVID-19
vaccines contain

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.100
animal-based ingredients?

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.010
SPEAKER 2: No, the manufacturing
process of the Moderna

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.850
and Pfizer BioNTech COVID-19
vaccines are cell-free,

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:50.090
and both vaccines contain
no human or animal products,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.270
preservatives, or adjuvants,
and utilize no ingredients

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:55.580
of human or animal origin.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.560
What else can I help you with?

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.570
SPEAKER 1: Am I eligible
for the COVID vaccine?

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.410
SPEAKER 2: The state's
prioritization strategy

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.420
for vaccine
distribution is designed

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.320
to ensure early vaccination of
the most vulnerable citizens.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.450
In order to determine
your eligibility,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.380
I will need to ask you
a series of questions.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.630
Let's get started.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.690
Are you a health care worker
in the ICU, ED, or EMS,

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.970
a long-term care facility
worker who regularly interacts

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.910
with residents, or a high-risk
long-term care facility

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:28.410
patient?

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.080
SPEAKER 1: No.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:31.800
SPEAKER 2: OK.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.040
Are you a first responder,
a teacher or school staff,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.980
a public health worker, an
essential frontline worker

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.130
that regularly interacts with
the public, a long-term care

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:43.290
facility patient,
or an individual

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.420
in the general
population at high risk

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.817
due to comorbidities
and health conditions?

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:49.400
SPEAKER 1: No.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:52.910
SPEAKER 2: Got it.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.190
Are you either
over 65 years old,

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:58.490
or under 65 years old with
high-risk comorbidities

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.247
and health conditions?

00:02:00.247 --> 00:02:00.830
SPEAKER 1: No.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.190
SPEAKER 2: OK.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.110
We're down to the
final question.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:09.517
Now, tell me, are you an
essential worker of any kind?

00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:10.100
SPEAKER 1: No.

00:02:12.595 --> 00:02:13.470
SPEAKER 2: Thank you.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.570
I have all the
information I need.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.030
The state has adopted
a multiphase approach

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.770
to vaccine distribution.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:23.250
Based on your responses, you
are eligible for the COVID-19

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.470
vaccine in phase 5.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.390
You can find
specific information

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.570
about vaccine availability
in the state's COVID-19

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:36.110
vaccination program document
at www.governor.state.gov.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:38.580
What else can I help you with?

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.795
SPEAKER 1: Where can I
get the COVID-19 vaccine?

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.480
SPEAKER 2: I'd be glad
to help with that.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.820
In order to find the
closest location where

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.160
you can get a vaccination,
please provide me

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.770
your five-digit zip code.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:58.720
SPEAKER 1: My zip code is 10011.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.470
SPEAKER 2: Got it.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.330
That's 10011.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.960
Based on this information, your
closest vaccination location

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.430
is Pharmacy A at 475
Sixth Avenue, New York.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:10.748
What else can I help you with?

00:03:10.748 --> 00:03:12.415
SPEAKER 1: Is there
some other location?

00:03:15.183 --> 00:03:16.600
SPEAKER 2: The
next location where

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:20.110
you can get a vaccine would
be Pharmacy B at 205 Eighth

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.940
Avenue, New York.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:23.892
What else can I help you with?

00:03:23.892 --> 00:03:27.820
SPEAKER 1: Actually, I
would prefer a hospital.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.480
SPEAKER 2: OK.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.970
The nearest hospital where
you can get the vaccine

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:36.040
is Medical Center C at 325
West 15th Street, New York.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:37.990
What else can I help you with?

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.120
SPEAKER 1: I want to
talk to a representative.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.140
SPEAKER 2: Sure.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.940
Please hold while
I transfer you.

00:03:54.682 --> 00:03:55.390
SPEAKER 3: Hello.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.580
Welcome to the State
Department of Health.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.140
How can I help you?

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.000
SPEAKER 1: Hey, so
I wanted to know,

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.680
will the vaccine give me COVID?

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:07.820
SPEAKER 3: No.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:09.710
None of the vaccines
being studied

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:13.897
are made of materials
that can cause disease.

00:04:13.897 --> 00:04:14.480
SPEAKER 1: OK.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.349
Can I get any allergic reaction
from the COVID-19 vaccine?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.030
SPEAKER 3: That's
a great question.

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.010
People can have
allergic reactions

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:34.420
to any medication or biological
products, such as a vaccine.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.593
Did I answer your question?

00:04:36.593 --> 00:04:37.510
SPEAKER 1: I think so.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.500
Thank you so much.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:42.560
SPEAKER 3: OK, thank you.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:43.220
Bye, bye.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.680
SPEAKER 1: Bye.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:48.160
What you just saw there was the
agent getting a recommendation

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.000
from the knowledge base for
the commonly-asked questions.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.440
They did not have to
look for the information.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:57.730
And there's also a
thumbs up or thumbs down,

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.700
which can be used by the
agent to provide feedback

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.160
to the system that
this response was good.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:08.840
This helps the Agent Assist to
incorporate the agent feedback.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:09.710
Thanks for watching.

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:12.400
And if you're looking for more
details on Contact Center AI

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:16.050
solution, we have
included the link below.

